ounds%20array%20behavior%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27For%20the%20retained%20conflicting%20array%20and%20string%20inputs%2C%20use%20the%20newer%20JavaScript%20behavior%20in%20both%20runtime%20packages%3A%20actual%20UTF-16%20code%20unit%20string%20lengths%20and%20observable%20out%20of%20bounds%20array%20reads%20remain%20part%20of%20the%20selected%20semantics.%20Preserve%20every%20original%20source%20input%2C%20including%20the%20complete%20ARRAYS%20corpus%20and%20the%20original%20string%20length%20source%2C%20and%20add%20genuine%20cross-runtime%20controls%20for%20supplementary%20Unicode%20and%20out%20of%20bounds%20reads%20rather%20than%20preserving%20obsolete%20contradictory%20native%20expectations.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27originalArrayAndStringInputsRetained%27%2C%20%27utf16StringLengthParityExecuted%27%2C%20%27observableOutOfBoundsParityExecuted%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-PARITY-OBSOLETE-NATIVE-EXPECTATIONS%27%2C%20%27evidence%20based%20correction%20of%20obsolete%20native%20array%20expectations%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Correct%20the%20obsolete%20Rust%20expectations%20identified%20in%20the%20captured%20question%20and%20answer%20to%20the%20newer%20JavaScript%20behavior%20while%20retaining%20all%20original%20test%20inputs%20and%20intended%20coverage.%20Record%20the%20actual%20contradictory%20before%20and%20after%20expectations%20and%20the%20active%20language%20or%20dependency%20context%3B%20genuine%20unsupported%20mutations%20and%20unrelated%20refusal%20boundaries%20remain%20required.%20Updating%20a%20wrong%20expectation%20is%20not%20permission%20to%20drop%20a%20fixture%2C%20hide%20a%20failed%20observation%20or%20claim%20unexecuted%20native%20parity.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27obsoleteExpectationConflictRecorded%27%2C%20%27correctedExpectationsFollowModernJavaScript%27%2C%20%27originalCoverageAndGenuineRefusalsRetained%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27compactContributorInstructionsRequest%27%2C%20compactContributorInstructionsSource%2C%20%27critical-conversation-requirements%27%2C%20%27contributor-instructions%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-CONTRIBUTOR-INSTRUCTIONS-CONCISE%27%2C%20%27minimal%20contributor%20instruction%20wording%20with%20unchanged%20obligations%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Reduce%20AGENTS.md%20and%20CLAUDE.md%20to%20the%20minimum%20practical%20wording%20while%20retaining%20the%20same%20substantive%20contributor%20obligations%20and%20the%20authoritative%20vision%20reference.%20Shared%20instructions%20may%20be%20referenced%20to%20avoid%20duplication%3B%20brevity%20does%20not%20remove%20implementation%2C%20evidence%2C%20resource%2C%20JavaScript-first%2C%20native%20CI%20or%20review%20obligations.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27contributorInstructionsReducedWithoutLostObligations%27%2C%20%27sharedInstructionsRemainAuthoritative%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ASSERTION-EVIDENCE-BASED-CORRECTION%27%2C%20%27demonstrably%20wrong%20assertions%20remain%20correctable%20without%20losing%20coverage%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Allow%20demonstrably%20wrong%20assertions%20and%20obsolete%20expected%20values%20to%20be%20corrected%20using%20recorded%20source%2C%20language%20or%20dependency%20evidence%20while%20preserving%20the%20original%20test%20inputs%2C%20genuine%20requirements%2C%20intended%20coverage%20and%20honest%20failure%20reporting.%20Record%20the%20reason%20and%20replacement%20expectation%2C%20update%20affected%20tests%20consistently%20and%20execute%20the%20corrected%20applicable%20assertions%3B%20a%20correction%20cannot%20excuse%20a%20real%20defect%2C%20weaken%20an%20acceptance%20obligation%20or%20stand%20in%20for%20execution%20evidence.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27wrongAssertionCorrectionSupportedByEvidence%27%2C%20%27originalInputsAndCoverageRetained%27%2C%20%27correctedApplicableAssertionsExecuted%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%5D%2C%20true%29%2C%0A%20%20...rows%28%27versionBoundedAssertionsRequest%27%2C%20versionBoundedAssertionsSource%2C%20%27critical-conversation-requirements%27%2C%20%27assertion-version-ranges%27%2C%20%5B%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ASSERTION-EXPLICIT-VERSION-RANGES%27%2C%20%27explicit%20applicable%20version%20ranges%20for%20version%20dependent%20assertions%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Every%20assertion%20whose%20expected%20behavior%20depends%20on%20a%20language%20or%20dependency%20version%20declares%20its%20version%20subject%2C%20explicit%20minimum%20and%20maximum%20bounds%2C%20endpoint%20inclusion%20and%20evidence%20for%20the%20expectation.%20Select%20and%20execute%20the%20expectation%20applicable%20to%20the%20actual%20active%20version%20instead%20of%20treating%20one%20historical%20result%20as%20valid%20for%20all%20versions%3B%20retain%20the%20original%20inputs%20and%20the%20recorded%20historical%20expectation.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27versionDependentExpectationsHaveExplicitBounds%27%2C%20%27activeVersionSelectsApplicableExpectation%27%2C%20%27historicalInputsAndExpectationsRetained%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ASSERTION-VERSION-COVERAGE%27%2C%20%27missing%20and%20conflicting%20active%20version%20expectation%20coverage%20refuses%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Require%20exactly%20one%20applicable%20expectation%20for%20an%20active%20version%20and%20validate%20every%20declared%20range%2C%20including%20inactive%20alternatives.%20Missing%20coverage%2C%20overlapping%20or%20conflicting%20ranges%2C%20malformed%20versions%20and%20ambiguous%20expectation%20identities%20fail%20explicitly%20rather%20than%20skipping%20the%20assertion%20or%20choosing%20an%20arbitrary%20alternative.%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%5B%27missingActiveVersionCoverageRefused%27%2C%20%27overlappingAndConflictingRangesRefused%27%2C%20%27allDeclaredRangesValidated%27%5D%5D%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%27I195-ASSERTION-LANGUAGE-EDITION-ORDER%27%2C%20%27declared%20language%20edition%20order%20distinct%20from%20release%20coordinates%27%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%27Compare%20dependency%20release%20coordinates%20with%20their%20explicit%20precision%2C%2